  "order": 1,
  "title": "Passé Composé with Avoir",
  "prerequisiteIds": ["fr-lesson-object-pronouns"],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "explanation", "markdown": "The **passé composé** is French's everyday past tense, similar to Italian's passato prossimo. Most verbs form it with **avoir** (conjugated) + a **past participle**: **J'ai mangé** (I ate). Regular **-er** verbs form their participle with **-é**: *manger* → **mangé**, *parler* → **parlé**." },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "fr-ex-pc-avoir-1" },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "fr-ex-pc-avoir-2" },
    { "type": "explanation", "markdown": "Some common verbs have irregular participles: *boire* → **bu**, *avoir* → **eu**, *être* → **été**." },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "fr-ex-pc-avoir-3" },
    { "type": "exercise", "exerciseId": "fr-ex-pc-avoir-4" }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "fr-ex-pc-avoir-1",
      "type": "fill-blank",
      "prompt": "J'___ mangé une pizza. (avoir — I ate a pizza.)",
      "answer": "ai",
      "relatedItemId": "fr-vocab-routine-004"
    },
    {
      "id": "fr-ex-pc-avoir-2",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "prompt": "What is the past participle of \"parler\" (to speak)?",
      "answer": "parlé",
      "distractors": ["parlait", "parler", "parlant"],
      "relatedItemId": "fr-vocab-routine-009"
    },
    {
